message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "OES-32 Dashboard: PyQt6 desktop view of a filtered synthetic 32-channel signal and its Welch PSD"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/oes32-dashboard"
url: "https://sparkainlpx.xyz"
abstract: >-
  OES-32 Dashboard is a self-contained PyQt6 + PyQtGraph desktop application
  that shows a rolling filtered waveform (channel 0) and a channel-averaged
  Welch power spectral density (0-50 Hz) for a simulated 32-channel signal.
  The GUI-free signal path (oes32_pipeline.py) applies a stateful 50 Hz IIR
  notch (Q = 30) and a 4th-order 0.5-45 Hz Butterworth bandpass at a nominal
  250 Hz. The synthetic input is a 10 Hz test tone plus a 50 Hz mains-like
  tone in arbitrary units. Scope: synthetic stimuli only. It is not hardware,
  field, medical or certified control software, makes no physical, biological
  or clinical claim, and is not the normative OES-32 residual (see
  oes32-residual).
keywords:
  - research software
  - signal processing
  - Welch PSD
